{
 "id": "surface_segmentation",
 "version": "1.0.0",
 "self_load_only": true,
 "depends_on": [
  "photon_retina"
 ],
 "latency_class": "hard_realtime",
 "description": "Mary's Room stage 4.3: colour-free surface segmentation of the 2-D photon sheet (GraphEye retina_2d + retina_2d_cones, adjacent_receptor edges). Luminance Y = L.caught_quanta + M.caught_quanta (no S, no opponent channel). Two adjacent cells are the SAME SURFACE iff |Y_a - Y_b| <= Sqrt(Y_a + Y_b): one standard deviation of the photon shot noise of the difference, a physical grain with no tuned multiplier (VISION_PROTOCOL sec 13). Components are found by the l4_flood min-label flood to the run_rules fixpoint; a per-epoch completion guard (SegmentationState.done_epoch) admits minting only after the fixpoint, then ONE SurfaceSegment{epoch, root, n_cells, has_boundary, current} per component, with cell -in_segment-> segment membership, and SegmentationState.final_epoch once every cell has joined. A component with no boundary (ganzfeld) has has_boundary=0 and is not a surface. Isoluminant chromatic edges are invisible to this criterion BY DESIGN (they merge; reported, not patched). Superseded segments are kept as history (current=0) with their live edges removed. Feeds surface_persistence, whose identity criterion is the track_comps cell overlap 2*ov >= min(count) (runners/dsl/src/substrate.rs track_comps). Flag SurfaceSegmentationParams.enabled, OFF by default (sec 9).",
 "microtheory": {
  "name": "surface_segmentation",
  "description": "luminance shot-noise edges -> connected surface segments"
 },
 "nodes": [
  {
   "local_id": 0,
   "type": "SurfaceSegmentationParams",
   "attrs": {
    "enabled": 0.0
   }
  },
